<title>HONG KONG: YGM explores U.S. listing of unit.</title>
<headline>YGM explores U.S. listing of unit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Garment and property firm YGM Trading Ltd said on Monday it was exploring the possibility of seeking a listing in the United States for its 63.92 percent owned ILC International Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;The company is presently exploring such possibilities, no plan to list ILC in the United States has been finalised and such plan may or may not materialise,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>ILC operates Hang Ten clothing stores in Taiwan and collects Hang Ten royalties worldwide, it said.</p>
<p>Shares of YGM were down HK$0.05 at HK$9.30 in late morning trade.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
